;; acme's downstream config — the THIRD-PARTY consumer's own context/skill
;; manifest, pointed at by `SEON_CONFIG=acme/config.edn` in `.env.acme`
;; (bin/acme sources it). This is the whole point of the env override: a
;; downstream consumer curates ITS agents' context WITHOUT editing seon src —
;; this manifest OVERRIDES seon's default `config/system.edn` for the acme
;; cluster only. Same schema as the default (`seon.config/manifest`); absent
;; keys fall through to the no-config defaults.
;;
;; Demonstrates a per-consumer override that visibly differs from the default
;; cluster: acme's agents always-load BOTH the datahike + repl skill bodies
;; (the default cluster loads only :repl), proving per-cluster control.
{:seon.config/loadouts
 [{:seon.config/role         :default
   :seon.config/default-load [:datahike :repl]}]}
